-- title:
--   Residue degree one for the ∞ Gauss branch of X₀(qM')
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain together with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ making $L$ a fraction field of $A$, and assume $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. Inside the Laurent series field $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ consider two intermediate fields over $L$: $K_0$, required to equal the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $\mathbb{Q}$-subfield of $\mathbb{Q}(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ generated by all quotients $\mathsf{q}$-expansion of $f$ divided by that of $g$, for modular forms $f,g$ of a common weight for $\Gamma_0(M')$ whose $\mathsf q$-expansions come from integral power series with the denominator series nonzero; and $K_0'$, required to equal the same construction for $\Gamma_0(qM')$. Assume $K_0 \le K_0'$. Let $O_0$ be a valuation subring of $K_0$ characterised by: $f \in O_0$ if and only if there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ after applying $A \to L$ coefficientwise; let $O_0'$ be a valuation subring of $K_0'$ characterised in the same way. Then every $f \in O_0'$ can be written as $f = g + m$ with $g \in O_0$ (included into $K_0'$) and $m$ a nonunit of $O_0'$.
--
--   This is the statement that the Gauss valuation ring of $A$-integral $\mathsf q$-expansions on the $\Gamma_0(qM')$-floor has the same residue field as the one on the $\Gamma_0(M')$-floor, i.e. residue degree one for the component of the special fibre through the cusp $\infty$; on $\mathsf q$-expansions this is the Kronecker congruence in residue characteristic $q$. It feeds the unramifiedness statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isUnramifiedAt_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul_comap_of_not_mem_ssJSet_xH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isUnramifiedAt_chartAlgFin_gamma0_mul_comap_of_not_mem_ssJSet_xH) for the corresponding chart of the model of the modular curve.
